{"name":"Stream Bed","hex":"#556061","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stream bed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of streambed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stream_bed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stream bed","blocks":[{"text":"A streambed or stream bed is the bottom of a stream or river and is confined within a channel or the banks of the waterway. Usually, the bed does not contain terrestrial (land) vegetation and instead supports different types of aquatic vegetation, depending on the type of streambed material and water velocity. Streambeds are what would be left once a stream is no longer in existence. The beds are usually well preserved even if they get buried because the banks and canyons made by the stream are typically hard, although soft sand and debris often fill the bed. Dry, buried streambeds can actually be underground water pockets. During times of rain, sandy streambeds can soak up and retain water, even during dry seasons, keeping the water table close enough to the surface to be obtainable by local people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Low_creek.jpg/330px-Low_creek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stream_bed"},{"title":"Stream","blocks":[{"text":"A stream is a continuous body of surface water flowing within the bed and banks of a channel. The channel is a watercourse, although the watercourse may be seasonally or periodically dry. Depending on its location or certain characteristics, a stream may be referred to by a variety of local or regional names. A long, large stream is usually called a river, while a smaller, less voluminous, and more intermittent stream is known as a creek or tributary, among other names."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/%D0%A6%D0%B2%D1%80%D1%86%D0%BA%D0%B0_2_PPRP001.jpg/330px-%D0%A6%D0%B2%D1%80%D1%86%D0%BA%D0%B0_2_PPRP001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stream"},{"title":"Bed","blocks":[{"text":"A bed is a piece of furniture that is used as a place to sleep, rest, and relax."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/2008-04-12_Freilichtmuseum_Detmold_%2811%29.jpg/330px-2008-04-12_Freilichtmuseum_Detmold_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bed"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Old_Mississippi_riverbed_near_St._Mary%27s.jpg/500px-Old_Mississippi_riverbed_near_St._Mary%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Old_Mississippi_riverbed_near_St._Mary%27s.jpg/1280px-Old_Mississippi_riverbed_near_St._Mary%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Old_Mississippi_riverbed_near_St._Mary%27s.jpg/500px-Old_Mississippi_riverbed_near_St._Mary%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The old bed of the Mississippi River near Kaskaskia, Illinois, left behind after the river shifted","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOld_Mississippi_riverbed_near_St._Mary's.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg/500px-Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg/1280px-Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg/500px-Potok_pod_jezerom_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse